WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:02.703
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh!

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.260
I am so bummed that I'm
not there in person.

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.500
You did such a great job in the film.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:12.630
I really, next time you come,

00:00:12.630 --> 00:00:14.730
I'm gonna give you such
a big hug. - Thank you.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:15.780
You're so talented.

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.970
And you just turned 21 right?

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.182
- I did. It was my 21st on the 20th.

00:00:21.182 --> 00:00:22.590
(audience applauding)

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.030
- Oh, that's a, that's a big thing.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.050
How did you celebrate?

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:25.883
- I know. Okay.

00:00:25.883 --> 00:00:26.760
Everybody keeps asking me,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:27.930
what are you gonna do for your 21st?

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:28.763
What are you gonna do?

00:00:28.763 --> 00:00:31.140
And I'm gonna be honest, it
was such an afterthought to me

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:33.390
because it was the week of like
the premiere of Disenchanted

00:00:33.390 --> 00:00:36.300
and it was genuinely like
the last thing on my mind.

00:00:36.300 --> 00:00:37.980
So, which always makes me laugh,

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.210
but when I was younger

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:41.070
I always used to celebrate
by going to Disney.

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:42.454
Ever since I was little,

00:00:42.454 --> 00:00:43.770
I was fortunate enough

00:00:43.770 --> 00:00:44.910
to have family out in California.

00:00:44.910 --> 00:00:46.380
And we'd go celebrate.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.170
And this year my Disneyland

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:52.010
was the premiere of Disenchanted. So...

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:55.260
- [Kelly] I mean, that's a pretty rad

00:00:55.260 --> 00:00:57.686
that's a pretty rad 21st birthday present.

00:00:57.686 --> 00:00:59.340
(laughing)

00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:01.230
So you play Morgan in the movie.

00:01:01.230 --> 00:01:02.790
You're all grown up, right?

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:03.623
- I do.

00:01:03.623 --> 00:01:04.456
- Or you're a teenager?

00:01:04.456 --> 00:01:05.289
- She's a teenager.

00:01:05.289 --> 00:01:06.150
She thinks she's all grown up,

00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:07.710
but she has a lot to learn.

00:01:07.710 --> 00:01:09.180
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:11.890
Well, most teenagers
think they're grown up.

00:01:11.890 --> 00:01:12.900
- Been there.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:15.840
- So, yeah, so we've all been there.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:17.790
But I thought you did such
a great job in the film.

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:20.440
It's such a, it's such a,
I always find it incredibly

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:23.580
an incredibly talented thing
to be able to act as well

00:01:23.580 --> 00:01:25.470
as you do as sing and dance.

00:01:25.470 --> 00:01:27.090
Like the whole thing is.

00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:29.610
And also, for people that
aren't into musical theater

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:30.960
I think they're going to love it

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:34.110
because it's like a
different kind of escapism.

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:35.400
It's not like,

00:01:35.400 --> 00:01:36.840
it's like you're, you're in on the joke

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.100
of almost breaking out into song.

00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:39.480
That's what I loved about Enchanted.

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.070
And that's what I loved
about Disenchanted.

00:01:41.070 --> 00:01:43.740
The storyline was brilliant

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:44.640
how it was played off.

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:47.790
And you almost got to play
two different Morgans.

00:01:47.790 --> 00:01:48.780
Like that's kind of cool.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.490
Like you got to play
two different versions

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:51.323
of your character.

00:01:51.323 --> 00:01:53.220
Was that kind of more
exciting as an actor?

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:55.020
- Yeah, I mean, it's
definitely a challenge

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:57.060
especially when Morgan becomes this

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:58.380
like fairytale character.

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:01.230
She's obviously like such the opposite

00:02:01.230 --> 00:02:02.700
of what we see her as this

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.650
jaded, sarcastic, bitter

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.560
in a sweet way kind of teenager.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:08.393
- Yeah.

00:02:08.393 --> 00:02:09.420
- So we see her totally
taken out of her element

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:11.820
and plopped into this fairytale universe.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.140
And it's kind of funny because

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:14.610
there's this stark contrast

00:02:14.610 --> 00:02:16.380
between her real personality

00:02:16.380 --> 00:02:18.600
and we almost see it sort of kind of

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:21.330
trickling into this
fairytale version of her,

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:24.930
especially when we get to
hear her sing her song Perfect

00:02:24.930 --> 00:02:26.430
about how that real bit

00:02:26.430 --> 00:02:27.840
of Morgan comes through
about that pressure

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:30.162
that she feels to kind of be perfect and

00:02:30.162 --> 00:02:32.520
and deliver and be this,

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.770
this epitomized version of

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:37.530
of what the people around
her believes she should be.

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:39.330
And I think everyone can kind of relate

00:02:39.330 --> 00:02:41.700
to that pressure to know
exactly who you should be

00:02:41.700 --> 00:02:42.930
and what you wanna do.

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:45.060
- Absolutely. I think
people can relate to that

00:02:45.060 --> 00:02:46.740
whether you're in the spotlight or not.

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:48.420
That's just something that comes with life

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:49.253
I feel like.

00:02:49.253 --> 00:02:51.360
You did, it was such a great job.

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:52.590
I mean, killer job.

00:02:52.590 --> 00:02:54.570
So you, you shot in London.

00:02:54.570 --> 00:02:56.670
I love London.

00:02:56.670 --> 00:02:59.809
I hear that the weather didn't
cooperate though, right?

00:02:59.809 --> 00:03:00.990
- No. It's so funny.

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:03.000
We saw this song called Perfect

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.980
about this perfect Monrolasia morning.

00:03:04.980 --> 00:03:05.910
And what was it doing?

00:03:05.910 --> 00:03:07.200
It was hailing all day.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:08.310
It was snowing all day.

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:10.920
Sleet, freezing rain. Um.

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:13.260
So, uh, what you see is

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.360
the little bit of the magic of Disney

00:03:15.360 --> 00:03:17.850
giving you bright blue sparkling skies

00:03:17.850 --> 00:03:19.812
on a cloudy,

00:03:19.812 --> 00:03:22.170
windy, stormy day.

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:23.400
And yeah. - Drab

00:03:23.400 --> 00:03:24.750
- Yeah, drab definitely.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:25.890
We were like rushed

00:03:25.890 --> 00:03:27.840
under tents every time it started hailing.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.770
And the second it would stop

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:29.640
they'd be like, oh, it's clear.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:30.473
It's clear.

00:03:30.473 --> 00:03:31.306
Everyone, everyone all right,

00:03:31.306 --> 00:03:32.340
pictures up and action.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:33.810
And we'd be like, it's
another perfect Monroe.

00:03:33.810 --> 00:03:35.640
Like just thrown right into it.

00:03:35.640 --> 00:03:37.800
- Wait I thought it was just like raining.

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:38.730
It was hailing?

00:03:38.730 --> 00:03:41.280
- Hailing. I had like a golf ball sized

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.370
like hailstone in my hand at one point.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:46.080
We tried to keep going
through it sometimes.

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:47.730
My director just didn't wanna call cut

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:49.140
cause it was like, we
got this, it's going.

00:03:49.140 --> 00:03:50.670
And all of a sudden he had
to because there were just

00:03:50.670 --> 00:03:53.490
hailstones bouncing off
my head in the shot.

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:54.600
And then a gust of wind

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:57.027
- You can like get a concussion from that.

00:03:57.027 --> 00:03:58.490
(laughing)

00:03:58.490 --> 00:04:00.240
- Anything for the magic.

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:02.310
- Oh my gosh.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.170
I, I just wanted to say you,

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:05.430
I'm so bummed I'm not there

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.710
cause literally, you, the whole cast

00:04:07.710 --> 00:04:10.276
y'all all did such a great job.

00:04:10.276 --> 00:04:11.220
It's sometimes hard, I feel like,

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:12.690
to do a sequel of something

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.070
so many people loved

00:04:14.070 --> 00:04:15.060
and were captivated by

00:04:15.060 --> 00:04:16.110
and loved in the first place.

00:04:16.110 --> 00:04:19.170
And I literally said this to
my executive producer, Alex.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.490
I watched it and I was like,

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.200
I loved it more than the first one,

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:23.790
which I didn't think was possible.

00:04:23.790 --> 00:04:25.740
It was so well done.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:27.570
And the storytelling was so cool

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:28.710
how they flipped it.

00:04:28.710 --> 00:04:30.300
We're such a fan of you.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:33.339
Please come back whenever
I can like hug you.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:34.660
- Thank you Kelly.

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:35.738
It was such an honor.

00:04:35.738 --> 00:04:36.936
- [Kelly] Yeah

00:04:36.936 --> 00:04:37.769
- Seriously.

00:04:37.769 --> 00:04:38.602
- Oh man, I'm such a fan.

00:04:38.602 --> 00:04:41.100
Everybody. You can see
Gabriela in Disenchanted.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:41.933
You're gonna wanna see it.

00:04:41.933 --> 00:04:43.233
It's on Disney Plus.

